   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## pbr-material.json\n\nMarigold-sourced PBR material set\n\n**Does:** one texture in -> albedo (basecolor), normal, roughness, metallic, AO and a glTF-valid **ORM** out. Marigold IID predicts the intrinsics; QFX turns them into maps. This is the graph version of `scripts/pbr_set.py`, and the two agree: the node's raw metallic (mean **0.359**, 0.5% of pixels > 0.5) matches the script's **0.354** within the run-to-run spread of the method itself (the script differs from its own re-run by 0.017 per pixel).\n**Why two Marigold loaders:** `MarigoldModelLoader` is stateful - the second load replaces the first - so each model gets its own loader + inference pair. Appearance gives albedo + material (roughness, metallic); lighting gives albedo + shading + residual, and QFX uses its index 1 as AO.\n**`albedo_source`:** `appearance` or `lighting` - both are legitimate albedos; pick the one that looks de-lit. `gamma_metal_rough 2.2` is what takes metallic from Marigold's ~0.36 down to ~0.11 in the packed output, so do not 'correct' it away.\n**The ORM output is glTF-ordered already** (R=occlusion, G=roughness, B=metallic - verified against the node's own Metallic output, byte-identical), so it drops straight into a glTF/engine material; the `metallicRoughness` slot and the `occlusion` slot share this one image by convention. No repacking step is needed. NB the channel swap that DOES matter is Unity's own shaders (R=metal, A=smoothness) - see PIPELINES open item 1.\n**Input:** `LoadImage` reads only ComfyUI's `input/`. Marigold wants ~768 px, so feed a seamless, power-of-two-ish square; the flow ships `2d/tex_stone_seamless.png` at 768.\n**Prefer `seamless_mode=off`** here: the source is already tileable (make it so first - `seamless-texture.json` with `method=offset`), and QFX's seamless crop shrinks the maps by 16 px per side, which then has to be tiled back up.\n**From here:** apply the maps to a mesh with `scripts/make_gltf_material.py --mesh <glb> --glb-out <glb>` (the mesh needs UVs - that is what `Hy3DMeshUVWrap` is for); `assets/3d/stone_statue.glb` is the worked example.\n\n---\n*Why it is this way: E25 (node route verified against U4), and the U4 entry in `2d/EXPERIMENTS-2D.md`.*"
   ],
   "title": "pbr-material"
  }
